# Round XXII Track δ regression: `r.map((int x): None())` on `Result[int,int]`
# — bare `None()` inside a Result.map closure body — must REJECT at check
# time. Class-sibling of `Option.map`; the receiver family is different but
# the underlying hole is the same NoneLiteral-call typechecker gap. Runtime
# observed at HEAD 0aa3f5a6 pre-fix: prints `Ok: 0`, both backends agreeing
# on wrong output (Core #8 both-wrong).
#
# Post-fix: same mechanism as the Option.map fixture — the closure typing at
# `typecheck.rs:7548` wraps Option[int] into Result[Option[int], int], which
# fails to unify with the outer Result[int, int] → E_TypeMismatch.
#
# COMBINATOR AXIS: .map (Result). Sibling
# `sound_bare_none_call_in_option_map_rejected.gg` covers Option.map.

void main():
    Result[int, int] r = Ok(3)
    Result[int, int] result = r.map((int x): None())
    if result is Ok(v): print(f"Ok: {v}") else: print("Error")
